Copyright (c) 2026 Rakvor. All rights reserved.

Software: RV Hub (rv-hub), including its source code, build scripts, tests, test data, documentation
and the executables built from them (the "Software").

1. Ownership. The Software is owned by Rakvor. No right is granted except as stated in this licence.

2. Use by Rakvor. Rakvor and its personnel may use, modify and build the Software to perform forensic,
   incident-response and security engagements. The Software is installed and run locally; it is not
   distributed, sold or offered as a service to third parties.

3. Audit right. A customer of Rakvor, a court, a party to proceedings in which results of the Software are
   relied upon, and an expert appointed by any of them (each an "Auditor") may, for the sole purpose of
   assessing the reliability of results produced by the Software in a specific matter:
   a) receive and inspect the source code of the version identified in the report concerned;
   b) build that version from source and compare the build with the published SHA256SUMS;
   c) run the Software, its self-test and its test suite, including on their own test data;
   d) quote limited extracts of the source code in expert reports and court filings for that matter.

4. Restrictions. An Auditor may not: distribute, publish, sublicense, sell or lend the Software or any
   part of it; use it for any purpose other than the audit in section 3; remove copyright or licence
   notices; or use it to provide services to others. Copies made for the audit must be deleted or returned
   when the matter ends, except where law or a court order requires their retention.

5. Third-party components. The Software includes or loads third-party components under their own licences
   (listed in NOTICE and the SBOM shipped with each release, e.g. PDFium under BSD-3-Clause, Rust crates and
   Python packages under MIT/Apache-2.0/BSD). Those licences govern those components and are not limited by
   this licence.

6. No warranty. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Results are technical
   signals interpreted by a qualified examiner; the Software does not issue legal conclusions. Every report
   states the Software's known limitations.

